WEBVTT

00:00:11.906 --> 00:00:12.606
Where the money is.

00:00:14.554 --> 00:00:16.431
A card payment is a journey with stages.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:18.351
First the bank says yes:

00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:19.759
that is the authorization.

00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:21.466
Then the money is claimed,

00:00:21.807 --> 00:00:23.258
and a few days later it settles.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:24.709
And sometimes it goes back:

00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:26.714
a refund, or a chargeback.

00:00:27.045 --> 00:00:27.941
For most of our payments,

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.202
the first two happen in one step.

00:00:33.607 --> 00:00:35.228
Approved has an exact meaning:

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:37.788
the bank sent back an authorization code.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.964
And not every request is a sale:

00:00:40.391 --> 00:00:42.268
some are only a check that the card works.

00:00:45.539 --> 00:00:46.392
Settlement comes later.

00:00:46.904 --> 00:00:49.464
On Worldpay, a sale reaches its settlement

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.128
date three days after the payment,

00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:53.688
and more than nine in ten within five days.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:54.920
One brand is different:

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.182
American Express pays us directly,

00:00:57.694 --> 00:00:59.571
so its sales never appear in that file.

00:01:03.013 --> 00:01:04.293
Money goes back in two ways.

00:01:04.805 --> 00:01:06.213
A refund, which we send:

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.218
about one and a half in every hundred

00:01:08.432 --> 00:01:09.132
approved orders.

00:01:09.456 --> 00:01:11.290
And a chargeback, which the bank takes:

00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:12.826
about one in seven hundred.

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:15.125
Refunds are made in the processors' own

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.642
consoles, so our payment record holds none

00:01:17.685 --> 00:01:18.385
of them.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.964
Each stage is written in a different record.

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:25.353
The bank's yes is in our payment service.

00:01:26.036 --> 00:01:27.615
The settlement is in the processor's files.

00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:29.620
A refund is in the order system.

00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:32.095
To follow one payment, we read all three.

00:01:35.318 --> 00:01:36.018
One last thing:

00:01:36.214 --> 00:01:38.688
an attempt that failed is not lost money.

00:01:39.158 --> 00:01:41.590
In one fault, sixty cards were declined;

00:01:42.059 --> 00:01:43.680
forty-five of them were approved again.

00:01:44.192 --> 00:01:46.070
And across the year, more than a million

00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:48.800
attempts were really fewer than a million decisions.

00:01:51.103 --> 00:01:51.803
Where the money is:

00:01:52.127 --> 00:01:55.241
authorized, settled, sometimes sent back,

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.415
and never counted as lost until we have looked.

